# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The repository root is ALSO an R package: the `TaxaID` meta-package, whose
# only job is to install the nine. Everything else in this repository is the
# monorepo around it -- the nine package sources, the development record, the
# release record, the generated prompt pack. None of that belongs inside the
# meta-package's own tarball, and leaving it in produced three R CMD check
# NOTEs plus a WARNING, which is why CI could not check this package at all.
# Nothing here is renamed or moved; this only scopes the BUILD.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# RStudio
^.*\.Rproj$
^\.Rproj\.user$
^\.Rprofile$

# The nine package sources. They are installed from their own directories,
# never from inside this tarball; shipping them here also drags in every
# per-package .Rbuildignore/.lintr (the "hidden files" NOTE) and every
# inst/CITATION (the "CITATION in a non-standard place" NOTE).
^TaxaTools$
^TaxaFetch$
^TaxaHabitat$
^TaxaMatch$
^TaxaLikely$
^TaxaExpect$
^TaxaAssign$
^TaxaFlag$
^TaxaWizard$

# Development and release records, and the generated prompt pack.
^ecosystem_docs$
^llm_prompts$
^usgs_release_review$
^CLAUDE\.md$
^code\.json$
^USGS_logo_green\.png$

# CI configuration and VCS
^\.github$
^\.git$
^\.gitignore$

# NOTE ON THIS FILE'S SYNTAX, learned the hard way: every line here is a
# PCRE regex, and R does NOT treat # as a comment. A "comment" is simply a
# regex that happens to match nothing -- so it must still COMPILE. An
# unbalanced parenthesis in prose makes R CMD build fail outright with
# "Build process failed", naming no line. Keep brackets out of these notes.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT ignored: DISCLAIMER.md and LICENSE.md stay in the build
# and leave one NOTE about non-standard top-level files. They exist ONLY at
# this root -- the nine packages had their copies removed when these were
# centralised here -- so excluding them would ship a USGS meta-package
# carrying neither its required disclaimer nor its licence text. A NOTE does
# not fail CI, because the gate is error_on = warning; a missing disclaimer
# would fail a USGS review.

# The two space-named review files under inst/ trip --as-cran's "non-portable
# file names" WARNING, and CI now fails on warnings. Deliberately NOT renamed:
# eight files reference these paths, and where development records live is an
# open question with the maintainer. Excluding them from this package's build
# is the narrow fix -- they stay in the repository, they just do not ship
# inside the tarball.
^inst/Code and Domain Review
